1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,108
If dragons existed,
your world's

2
00:00:02,128 --> 00:00:04,133
architecture would
look very different.

3
00:00:04,153 --> 00:00:06,308
Because this is what
a dragon sees.

4
00:00:06,328 --> 00:00:08,388
Every thatch roof,
open pen and cart:

5
00:00:08,408 --> 00:00:09,270
a target.

6
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:10,278
Press run.

7
00:00:10,298 --> 00:00:11,774
Week one:
roofs burn.

8
00:00:11,794 --> 00:00:13,324
Week two:
flocks gone.

9
00:00:13,344 --> 00:00:15,376
Week three:
nobody travels.

10
00:00:15,396 --> 00:00:16,576
Nobody fought a war.

11
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:18,516
They just lived in
plain sight.

12
00:00:18,536 --> 00:00:19,603
So hide the village.

13
00:00:19,623 --> 00:00:20,966
Four changes are
easy.

14
00:00:20,986 --> 00:00:22,527
The fifth is the
twist.

15
00:00:22,547 --> 00:00:23,514
One:
roofs.

16
00:00:23,534 --> 00:00:25,102
Slate and turf don't
burn.

17
00:00:25,122 --> 00:00:26,013
Two:
pens.

18
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:27,800
Flocks sleep in
covered barns.

19
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:28,818
Three:
place.

20
00:00:28,838 --> 00:00:30,594
Build in the valley,
under the cliff.

21
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:31,631
Four:
travel.

22
00:00:31,651 --> 00:00:33,363
Move at night,
under the trees.

23
00:00:33,383 --> 00:00:34,349
Run it again.

24
00:00:34,369 --> 00:00:35,492
The dragon looks
down,

25
00:00:35,512 --> 00:00:36,738
and finds nothing.

26
00:00:36,758 --> 00:00:37,463
Rule five?

27
00:00:37,483 --> 00:00:38,391
Look back.

28
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:40,533
A watchtower sees
the dragon first.

29
00:00:40,553 --> 00:00:42,679
One bell,
and everyone hides.

30
00:00:42,699 --> 00:00:44,565
Whoever rings it
runs the village.

31
00:00:44,585 --> 00:00:46,745
The dragon changed
who's in charge.

32
00:00:46,765 --> 00:00:48,231
Don't just add a
dragon.

33
00:00:48,251 --> 00:00:49,744
Ask what ordinary
people do

34
00:00:49,764 --> 00:00:50,694
differently.

35
00:00:50,714 --> 00:00:51,987
What would your
civilization invent

36
00:00:52,007 --> 00:00:53,449
to survive dragons?

37
00:00:53,469 --> 00:00:54,622
Comment below.

38
00:00:54,642 --> 00:00:56,436
Part 27 of 50.

39
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:58,586
Follow for part 28:
something on the

40
00:00:58,606 --> 00:01:00,248
Isle learns to build.
